Generate Claude-optimized project orientation context.

By default, outputs a lean orientation (~5k tokens) with project metadata,
key symbols, packages, conventions, and active work context.

Use --full for the complete architecture dump with all components, data flows,
boundaries, and files organized by concern.

Examples:
  snipe context                    # Claude-optimized orientation (default)
  snipe context --orient           # Same — explicit orientation mode
  snipe context --full             # Full architecture dump
  snipe context --format=yaml      # Output as YAML
  snipe context --conventions      # Coding conventions only

Usage:
  snipe context [path] [flags]

Flags:
      --conventions     Detect coding conventions
      --format string   Structured output format: json or yaml (default: claudish text)
      --full            Full architecture dump (all components, flows, boundaries)
  -h, --help            help for context
      --orient          Claude-optimized orientation (default)
      --output-nug      Output as Orca nugget YAML (for save_nug)

Global Flags:
      --context int        Context lines around match (default 2)
      --kg-hints           Include Orca KG hints
      --limit int          Cap results (default 10)
      --max-tokens int     Token budget (0 = unlimited)
      --no-body            Exclude function body
      --no-siblings        Exclude sibling declarations
      --offset int         Pagination offset
      --select string      Result selection: all, best, top3, top5 (default "all")
      --signature-only     Return only signature (no body, no context)
      --suggestions        Include next-step suggestions in Claude output
      --timeout duration   Timeout for command (e.g., 30s, 5m)
